 "min_length_ratio": 0.5,
 "notes": "Scale words are Brazilian: bilhão is 10^9. In Portugal bilião means 10^12, so the unknown-scale rule blocks it. deve is must; should is always deveria, never deve. Negation is read within three words before and one after a modal: não exige is need-not, não se deve is must-not. um and uma are not number words (they are the article) except inside compounds. se is not a clause break: não se deve keeps its negation.",
